  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-plugin-verify",
      "text": "**Verification toolkit for DeepSeek Harness agents** — evidence-based claim checking, config validation, and read-only network probes (URL / npm / GitHub)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "Tool schemas are validated against the `@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools` value-schema DSL at plugin load (checked against dsh-tools 0.1.0-rc.6 and 0.1.1-rc.2). Earlier releases used JSON-Schema `required` at the root of `output.schema` and closed nested objects without declared properties, which made the host abort the whole profile boot with `unsupported JSON schema: schema.required is not supported by the value schema DSL` and could reject the tool's own results. Current releases fix both; if an affected version left your DSH unable to start, remove the plugin from the profile (or upgrade) — no data is lost."
    },
    {
      "section": "Tools",
      "text": "| Tool | Mode | What it does |\n|---|---|---|\n| `verify` | `claim` | Verify a statement against workspace files: keyword extraction, per-keyword hits with **line-level citations**, verdict `verified` / `partial` / `unsupported` |\n| | `config` | Validate a config file — JSON strict parse or YAML structural smoke check |\n| | `url` | HTTP(S) availability: status, redirect target, latency |\n| | `npm` | Registry check: exists, latest version, `dsh.bundle` manifest, publish time |\n| | `repo` | GitHub submission-readiness: exists, age, `dsh-plugin` topic, approximate commit count |\n| | `batch` | Run many checks at once (`claims` / `configs` / `urls` / `packages` / `repos`) with bounded concurrency, a summary table and a per-result confidence grade |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "```\nverify claim \"the plugin pins zod in dependencies\"           # evidence search in workspace\nverify claim \"this repo has 12 commits\" scope ./some-dir\nverify config ./cordis.patch.yml\nverify url https://example.com"
    },
    {
      "section": "Notes",
      "text": "- Read-only: never writes files, never executes scanned content.\n- Claim verification is a heuristic (keyword evidence), not proof — an `unsupported` verdict means \"no evidence found\", treat it as unconfirmed.\n- YAML check is a structural smoke check (balanced quotes/brackets, indentation), not a full YAML parser."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```bash\nnode --check lib/*.js\nnode test/verify.test.mjs\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    },
    {
      "section": "Roadmap",
      "text": "See [ROADMAP.md](./ROADMAP.md) — next five versions (v1.1.0 – v1.5.0): batch & confidence, reports & regression, strict validation, probe hardening, submission-readiness expansion."
    }
  ],
